@startuml public_chat_event_boundary
title Public Chat Events Boundary
skinparam shadowing false

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@7e54b47f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java submitEvent/listEvents
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@7e54b47f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java projection methods
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@7e54b47f modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAIResponsesProvider.java handleOutputItemAdded/handleOutputItemDone/convertToolResultInput
' Observed behavior: the current Claw HTTP layer has request-scoped POST SSE and history GET, but no independent long-lived stream GET.
' Observed identity: OpenAI Responses call_id maps to Claw ToolCall.id and is written back for Tool results.
' Target-only design: Mate separates event submission, live Chat observation, and authoritative fixed-snapshot history.
' Design reason: a transport disconnect must not determine whether a write succeeded or whether an execution continues.
' Architecture change: Mate publishes the OpenAI Tool Call ID unchanged while keeping eventId independent.

actor "Authorized client" as Client
component "mate-service\nChat Events API" as Mate
component "Private Chat to Session\nresolver" as Resolver
component "CampusClaw\nSession runtime" as Claw
database "Authoritative\nevent history" as History

Client -> Mate : POST /chats/{chatId}/events
Mate -> Mate : authenticate and authorize Chat
Mate -> Resolver : resolve private Session
Resolver --> Mate : sessionId
Mate -> Claw : submit one user event
Claw -> History : persist accepted event
Mate --> Client : eventId and createdAt

Client -> Mate : GET /chats/{chatId}/events/stream
Claw --> Mate : normalized live domain events
Mate --> Client : data-only SSE from connection time

note right of Mate
OpenAI Responses call_id becomes Claw ToolCall.id.
Mate publishes it unchanged as toolCallId.
Mate eventId remains a separate event identity.
end note

Client -> Mate : GET /chats/{chatId}/events
Mate -> History : read fixed snapshot
History --> Mate : complete durable events
Mate --> Client : ResultBean page
@enduml

@startuml public_chat_event_recovery
title Live Stream and Durable History Reconciliation
skinparam shadowing false

' Public evidence: Claude Managed Agents events-and-streaming docs, checked 2026-09-02.
' Source evidence: pi@5cd93f68 packages/protocol/src/schemas.ts TranscriptProgressSchema/SessionSnapshotSchema
' Source evidence: pi@5cd93f68 packages/server/src/sessions.ts handleRuntimeEvent/broadcastSnapshot
' Design reason: deltas are disposable preview while completed history is authoritative.
' Architecture change: public eventId replaces exposure of internal sequence for reconciliation.

participant Client
participant "Mate live stream" as Stream
participant "Mate history API" as Query
participant "CampusClaw runtime" as Claw

Client -> Stream : open Chat SSE
Client -> Claw : submit user.message through Mate
Claw --> Stream : agent.message delta, same eventId
Stream --> Client : data JSON preview
Claw --> Stream : agent.message completed, same eventId
Stream --> Client : data JSON authoritative completion

... network disconnect ...

Client -> Stream : reopen Chat SSE
Client -> Query : GET history with createdAtGte
Query --> Client : fixed snapshot page
Client -> Client : deduplicate by eventId
Client -> Client : replace preview with completed event

loop while nextPage exists
  Client -> Query : GET history with opaque page only
  Query --> Client : next fixed-snapshot page
end

note over Client,Claw
Never replay an uncertain POST automatically.
An SSE disconnect does not cancel the execution.
New history polling starts with inclusive createdAtGte.
end note
@enduml
